%[text] # comp.Driver Class
%[text] **J.G. Vermond, JVsound**
%[text] Loudspeaker driver, described by its Thiele-Small parameters and the limits of its datasheet.
%[text] **Namespace:** comp
%[text] **Superclasses:** none
%%
%[text] ## Description
%[text] The `comp.Driver` class describes the electromechanical transducer of a loudspeaker system. The Thiele-Small parameters `Re`, `Le`, `Qes`, `Qms`, `Fs`, `Sd` and `Vas` of the datasheet set the electrical, electromechanical and mechanical side of the two-port network of [`lspsys`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','lspsys','lspsysdoc.m'))); the other parameters, such as `Bl`, `Cms` and `Mmd`, are derived from them.
%[text] The limits of the datasheet, the power handling with its impedances and the excursion, are optional: they do not change the calculation, and a limit of 0 means that it is not given. [`result.splMax`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','result','resultdoc.m'))) uses them to calculate the highest sound pressure level; `ExcursionLimit` and `PowerLimit` choose which limits it uses by default.
%%
%[text] ## Creation
%[text] ```matlabCodeExample
%[text] obj = comp.Driver
%[text] ```
%[text] Creates a driver with all parameters set to 0, which means not given for the optional limits, and the limit choice `ExcursionLimit = "Xvar"` and `PowerLimit = "Pnom"`. Set the parameters of the datasheet before you use the driver.
%%
%[text] ## Properties
%[text] The properties are listed in the order of the class definition file.
%%
%[text] ### `Re` — Resistance of the voice coil
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[Ohm\]
%[text] DC resistance $ R\_e $ of the voice coil. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0.
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Le` — Inductance of the voice coil
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[H\]
%[text] Inductance $ L\_e $ of the voice coil. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0.
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Qes` — Electrical Q
%[text] `(1,1) double`
%[text] Electrical quality factor $ Q\_{es} $ at the resonance frequency. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0.
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Qms` — Mechanical Q
%[text] `(1,1) double`
%[text] Mechanical quality factor $ Q\_{ms} $ at the resonance frequency. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0.
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Fs` — Resonance frequency
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[Hz\]
%[text] Resonance frequency $ f\_s $ of the driver in free air. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0.
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Sd` — Effective area of the diaphragm
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[m2\]
%[text] Effective area $ S\_d $ of the diaphragm. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0.
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Vas` — Equivalent suspension volume
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[m3\]
%[text] Volume $ V\_{as} $ of air with the same compliance as the suspension. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0.
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Znom` — Nominal impedance
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[Ohm\]
%[text] Optional. Nominal impedance $ Z\_{nom} $ of the datasheet. `Paes2012` is calculated with it. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0 (not given).
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Zmin` — Minimum impedance
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[Ohm\]
%[text] Optional. Lowest impedance $ Z\_{min} $ in the working range of the driver. `Pnom`, `Pcont` and `Paes1984` are calculated with it. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0 (not given).
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Pnom` — Nominal power handling
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[W\]
%[text] Optional. Nominal power handling $ P\_{nom} $ of the datasheet. B&C measures it after AES2-1984: pink noise with a crest factor of 6 dB in the working range, for 2 hours, with the power calculated with `Zmin`. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0 (not given).
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Pcont` — Continuous power
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[W\]
%[text] Optional. Continuous (program) power $ P\_{cont} $ of the datasheet, calculated with `Zmin`. B&C defines it as 3 dB above the nominal power, twice `Pnom`, as a recommended amplifier power for music. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0 (not given).
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Paes1984` — Power handling after AES2-1984
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[W\]
%[text] Optional. Power handling $ P\_{AES,1984} $ after AES2-1984: pink noise with a crest factor of 6 dB, for 2 hours, with the power calculated with `Zmin`. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0 (not given).
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Paes2012` — Power handling after AES2-2012
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[W\]
%[text] Optional. Power handling $ P\_{AES,2012} $ after AES2-2012 (reaffirmed 2023): pink noise with a crest factor of 12 dB, with the power calculated with `Znom`. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0 (not given).
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Xmax` — Maximum linear excursion
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[m\]
%[text] Optional. Maximum linear excursion $ X\_{max} $ of the diaphragm, one way. B&C gives it as a mathematical value from the height of the voice coil and the magnetic gap. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0 (not given).
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Xvar` — Excursion at 50 % of Bl or Cms
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[m\]
%[text] Optional. Excursion $ X\_{var} $ of the diaphragm, one way, where the force factor $ Bl $, the compliance $ C\_{ms} $ or both fall to less than 50 % of their small-signal value, as B&C defines it. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0 (not given).
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Xlim` — Excursion limit
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[m\]
%[text] Optional. Excursion limit $ X\_{lim} $ of the diaphragm, one way, as the datasheet gives it. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0 (not given).
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Xmech` — Mechanical excursion limit
%[text] `(1,1) double` \[m\]
%[text] Optional. Mechanical excursion limit $ X\_{mech} $ of the diaphragm, one way, as the datasheet gives it. Must be nonnegative. Default: 0 (not given).
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `ExcursionLimit` — Excursion limit for the maximum level
%[text] `(1,1) string`
%[text] Name of the excursion limit that `lspsys.createResult` copies to `result.ExcursionLimit`, the default limit of `result.splMax`: `"Xmax"`, `"Xvar"`, `"Xlim"` or `"Xmech"`. Default: `"Xvar"`.
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `PowerLimit` — Power limit for the maximum level
%[text] `(1,1) string`
%[text] Name of the power limit that `lspsys.createResult` copies to `result.PowerLimit`, the default limit of `result.splMax`: `"Pnom"`, `"Pcont"`, `"Paes1984"` or `"Paes2012"`. Default: `"Pnom"`.
%[text] **Attributes:** `GetAccess = public`, `SetAccess = public`
%%
%[text] ### `Bl` — Force factor
%[text] `double` \[Tm\]
%[text] Product of the magnetic field in the air gap and the length of the wire in it, from the electrical Q: $ Bl = \\sqrt{\\frac{R\_e}{2 \\pi f\_s Q\_{es} C\_{ms}}} $.
%[text] **Attributes:** `Dependent`
%%
%[text] ### `Cms` — Compliance of the suspension
%[text] `double` \[m/N\]
%[text] Mechanical compliance of the suspension, from the equivalent volume: $ C\_{ms} = \\frac{V\_{as}}{\\rho c^2 S\_d^2} $.
%[text] **Attributes:** `Dependent`
%%
%[text] ### `Mmd` — Mass of the diaphragm and the voice coil
%[text] `double` \[kg\]
%[text] Moving mass without the air load on both sides: $ M\_{md} = M\_{ms} - 2 M\_{mi} $. The enclosure adds the air load back.
%[text] **Attributes:** `Dependent`
%%
%[text] ### `Mms` — Moving mass including the air load
%[text] `double` \[kg\]
%[text] Moving mass in free air, from the resonance frequency: $ M\_{ms} = \\frac{1}{(2 \\pi f\_s)^2 C\_{ms}} $.
%[text] **Attributes:** `Dependent`
%%
%[text] ### `Mmi` — Air load on one side
%[text] `double` \[kg\]
%[text] Mass of the air load on one side of a piston in an infinite baffle: $ M\_{mi} = 2.67 \\rho r\_d^3 $.
%[text] **Attributes:** `Dependent`
%%
%[text] ### `Rms` — Mechanical resistance of the suspension
%[text] `double` \[Ns/m\]
%[text] Mechanical resistance, from the mechanical Q: $ R\_{ms} = \\frac{1}{Q\_{ms}} \\sqrt{\\frac{M\_{ms}}{C\_{ms}}} $.
%[text] **Attributes:** `Dependent`
%%
%[text] ### `DiaphragmRadius` — Radius of the diaphragm
%[text] `double` \[m\]
%[text] Radius of a circle with the effective area: $ r\_d = \\sqrt{S\_d / \\pi} $.
%[text] **Attributes:** `Dependent`
%%
%[text] ### `Qts` — Total Q
%[text] `double`
%[text] Total quality factor $ Q\_{ts} = \\frac{Q\_{es} Q\_{ms}}{Q\_{es} + Q\_{ms}} $.
%[text] **Attributes:** `Dependent`
%%
%[text] ## Methods
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[120,100,-1]}
%[text] | Method | Type | Description |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text] | [`zeb`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','comp','driver','methods','zebdoc','zebdoc.m'))) | Instance | Blocked electrical impedance $ Z\_{eb} = R\_e + j \\omega L\_e $ at frequencies `f`. |
%[text] | [`zm`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','comp','driver','methods','zmdoc','zmdoc.m'))) | Instance | Mechanical impedance $ Z\_m $ of the moving system at frequencies `f`. |
%[text] | [`te`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','comp','driver','methods','tedoc','tedoc.m'))) | Instance | Transmission matrix $ \\mathbf{T}\_e $ of the electrical side at frequencies `f`. |
%[text] | [`tbl`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','comp','driver','methods','tbldoc','tbldoc.m'))) | Instance | Transmission matrix $ \\mathbf{T}\_{bl} $ of the electromechanical transduction. |
%[text] | [`tm`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','comp','driver','methods','tmdoc','tmdoc.m'))) | Instance | Transmission matrix $ \\mathbf{T}\_m $ of the mechanical side at frequencies `f`. |
%[text] | [`tsd`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','comp','driver','methods','tsddoc','tsddoc.m'))) | Instance | Transmission matrix $ \\mathbf{T}\_{sd} $ of the effective diaphragm area. |
%[text:table]
%%
%[text] ## Examples
%%
%[text] ### Example: Driver of a datasheet
%[text] Create a B&C 21SW152-8 with the Thiele-Small parameters and the limits of its datasheet, and show its derived parameters.
%[text] ![](text:image:5181)
d = comp.Driver;
d.Re = 6;
d.Le = 2.2e-3;
d.Qes = 0.38;
d.Qms = 6.4;
d.Fs = 32;
d.Sd = 1680e-4;
d.Vas = 200e-3;
d.Znom = 8;
d.Zmin = 7;
d.Pnom = 2000;
d.Pcont = 4000;
d.Xmax = 15e-3;
d.Xvar = 16e-3;
derived = table(d.Bl,d.Cms,d.Mms,d.Mmd,d.Rms,d.Qts,VariableNames=["Bl","Cms","Mms","Mmd","Rms","Qts"]) %[output:0acd4a48]

